## 2. Purpose-Relative Fidelity for Logic

GFF-1's core insight is that **fidelity is purpose-relative**. This applies directly to Organic Logic:

| Purpose | Appropriate Logic | Why |
|:---|:---|:---|
| Static, closed systems (e.g., mathematics) | **Classic Logic** | Binary truth, no contradictions allowed |
| Dialectical critique | **Anti-Logic** | Opposition and negation emphasized |
| Living, organic systems | **Organic Logic** | Handles contradiction, emergence, change |

**The principle:** No single logic is universally faithful. The appropriate logic depends on the **purpose** for which it is employed. Organic Logic is faithful for the purpose of representing living systems. Classic Logic is faithful for the purpose of representing static, formal systems.

